WEBVTT

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:20.090
25 years ago, deep in the heart of Alabama, they built a speedway unlike any other.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:24.740
Her steep banking invites cars to the unforgiving concrete walls that surround her.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:29.850
She has accepted the challenge of the best, but only twice could the king raise his specter.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:39.460
Richard Petty remembers how NASCAR Winston Cup racing used to be when the driver was called upon to do more than just steer the car around the tri-oval.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:49.310
We all remember the drivers who lived with Interstate and established a group led by Bobby Allison called the Alabama Gang.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:59.860
Now a new generation of drivers and owners seek a spot in the history books and for some a chance to rise to the level of the original members.

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:05.210
In her 25-year history, the sport has changed so much.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:09.690
The racing has evolved, and so has the work on Pit Road.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:20.160
The ballet of yesterday has been changed into a science

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.600
which pushes crews to the edge of excellence.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:39.300
The history of this palace of speed has called upon all competitors to live on the edge every second of the journey.

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:57.000
They come through the triomal. Checkered is waving. Ernie Irvin wins and Rusty spins and gets airborne.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.900
So much has changed in the past quarter of a century.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.780
yet one thing has remained the same.

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:04.010
Talladega continues to mean speed

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:06.070
and the Oliva Challenge for drivers.

